EC2 WITH MORE FILES:

1. Launch EC2 Instance
AMI: Ubuntu Server 22.04 LTS (Free Tier eligible)
Instance type: t2.micro
Security Group (SG):
Type	Port	Source
SSH	22	Your IP
HTTP	80	0.0.0.0/0
Key Pair: Create or use an existing one → download .pem file
Launch the instance and note its Public IPv4 address

2. Connect to the Instance
Use EC2 Instance Connect or SSH from terminal:
ssh -i "my-key.pem" ubuntu@<PUBLIC_IP>

3. Update and Install Apache
sudo apt update -y
sudo apt install apache2 -y
sudo systemctl start apache2
sudo systemctl enable apache2

Check Apache status:
sudo systemctl status apache2

4. Upload Website Files
From your local system, upload your HTML, CSS, and JS files:
scp -i "my-key.pem" login.html style.css script.js ubuntu@<PUBLIC_IP>:/tmp/

Then move them into Apache’s web root:
sudo mv /tmp/*.html /var/www/html/
sudo mv /tmp/*.css /var/www/html/
sudo mv /tmp/*.js /var/www/html/
sudo cp /var/www/html/login.html /var/www/html/index.html
sudo chmod 644 /var/www/html/*
sudo systemctl restart apache2

5. Verify Access
In your browser, open:
http://<PUBLIC_IP>/
You should see your login page.
If not:
Check Security Group → make sure HTTP (80) is allowed.
Verify Apache is active:
sudo systemctl status apache2
Check logs if needed:
sudo tail -n 20 /var/log/apache2/error.log

6. (Optional) Auto-setup using User Data
To automate Apache install and hosting on every new instance:
Add this under Advanced details → User data during launch:
#!/bin/bash
apt update -y
apt install apache2 -y
systemctl start apache2
systemctl enable apache2
echo "<h1>Welcome to My Static Site</h1>" > /var/www/html/index.html

7. Final Verification
Apache status: active (running)
curl localhost inside instance shows your page
http://<PUBLIC_IP>/ opens your site publicly
